      "writtenOn": "2022-10-28T23:51:01Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e The race I was thinking of is with `activate_task()`.\n\nI see. I think we can address that by changing `freezer_do_not_count()` to use release semantics to write to `current-\u003eflags`. This should ensure that the write to `on_rq` in `activate_task()` will not be reordered after the write to `flags`. Precompiled modules will continue to use relaxed semantics, but given the unlikelihood of observing the wrong ordering, perhaps we can live with that.\n\n\u003e I think we should try very hard to preserve the upstream behaviour for systems which don\u0027t have the asymmetric misfeature.\n\nDone.",
